WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
- So I always like to wrap
things up with something cool

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.070
or unusual from social
media. But this week,

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.770
instead of sharing what I
am liking, we are leaving it

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.860
to the viewers, highlighting
our most viral moments ever.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.571
So this is what you're liking.

00:00:12.571 --> 00:00:14.859
(upbeat, happy music)

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:15.780
- {Audience} Woooo!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.480
- This one goes back to a
very cool hour when I got to

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.650
hang out with the one and
only Dave Grohl. I love him.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.260
Obviously, we talked a lot
about music, and he revealed

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.247
something that really surprised
me about one of his songs.

00:00:28.247 --> 00:00:29.220
(Audience claps)

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.530
One of your most popular songs
is "Learn to Fly". I love it.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.861
You wrote on it, "Looking
to the sky to save me,

00:00:33.861 --> 00:00:36.060
looking for a sign of life,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.950
looking for something to
help me burn out bright."

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.450
Now this is, once again, it comes back

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.710
to that whole thing
that I love that you do.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.050
For me, whenever I'm
listening to your lyrics,

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.121
maybe you didn't write it like this,

00:00:44.121 --> 00:00:47.040
but I love that soaring feeling

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.600
like that whole thing I get like visually.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.280
I always love your lyrics
too, because it's like paint.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:52.020
You paint such a great visual for me.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.582
And I love that.

00:00:53.582 --> 00:00:55.680
But it kind of, again, to me is like

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.940
a little dark and a little light.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.910
It's always there, like a shared world

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.113
which I guess is life.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.330
- I don't wanna burst your bubble.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.280
- Okay. I'm gonna drink my tea.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.743
And you're like, so this was about

00:01:06.743 --> 00:01:08.173
- At the time I wanted to become a pilot.

00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:10.354
I was like, I wanted to learn to fly.

00:01:10.354 --> 00:01:12.483
Like, I did. I mean,

00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:13.980
like that's it.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.150
Like, I was like,

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.053
I was,

00:01:17.507 --> 00:01:18.349
I hate that.

00:01:18.349 --> 00:01:19.182
- Oh!

00:01:19.182 --> 00:01:20.777
I know, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:01:20.777 --> 00:01:21.610
- Oh my God!

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:22.663
- I got these video tapes.

00:01:22.663 --> 00:01:23.521
- It's so literal!

00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:24.354
- I was reading all these books.

00:01:24.354 --> 00:01:25.187
- It really is.

00:01:25.187 --> 00:01:26.020
- It's so literal.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:26.853
- I'm sorry.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.686
- Oh my God.

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:28.519
- I'm sorry.

00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:29.589
- Oh my God. And in my brain,

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.450
- It's what I'm talking about!

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.572
- I'm singing it because I
wanna learn how to be a pilot

00:01:31.572 --> 00:01:32.405
- In my brain

00:01:32.405 --> 00:01:34.200
- You're singing it because like I'm

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.454
so inspired by life and whatever.

00:01:35.454 --> 00:01:36.330
(Audience laughs)

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:37.163
See!

